      "content": "Thanks for this. It’s a good start and it definitely doesn't sound hysterical, which I appreciate. \n\nHowever, looking at the internal score, it's a bit lower than I'd like. It's coming in pretty low on those urgency markers we discussed. I'm worried that if the email is *too* clinical, people might just scroll past it thinking it's just another scientific report.\n\nCould we do another version? I really want to boost that sense of urgency throughout the text. Just please keep an eye on the tone—I'm still very wary of it sounding like \"crisis-porn\" or losing its credibility. We want them to feel the weight of the situation, not think we're being dramatic for the sake of it. Can you try to integrate those urgency keywords more effectively?",
